\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec0 Track running \
For a given number of weeks we have measured the lap times of an amateur \
athlete running track. \
Write a program that decides whether the athlete kept continuously \
improving their total time! \
Input \
The first line of the standard input contains the count of weeks (2\uc0\u8804 n\u8804 10) \
when we measured the performance of the athlete and the number of laps \
(1\uc0\u8804 m\u8804 10) they ran each week. The next n lines contain the individual m \
number of lap times (30\uc0\u8804 t\u8804 60) on a given week the sum of which represents \
the total running time on that week. \
Output \
The first line of the standard output should contain a Boolean value \
representing whether or not the total running time each week kept \
decreasing. \
Example 1 \
Input Output \
4 4 \
51 52 53 59 \
52 52 51 55 \
51 54 56 59 \
50 51 49 53 \
 \
false \
Example 2 \
Input Output \
3 3 \
50 49 51 \
49 49 50 \
50 46 48 \
true \
